        "market_heading": "Why virtual home staging matters in today’s Chicago market",
        "market_text": "<p>Chicago's signature stock — vintage condos, greystones and two-flats — photographs with beautiful bones and empty, echoing rooms. Home staging warms the vintage details buyers love while proving the rooms hold modern furniture, the doubt that stalls showings on older stock.</p><p>With 97% of buyers starting their search online (NAR), the listing photos are the first impression most potential buyers get — and an empty vintage room rarely makes a memorable one. Staging makes a home visually distinctive online and highlights the features and appeal buyers are paying for.</p><p>Chicago is also fiercely seasonal: listings that launch in spring market weeks compete with everything else that waited for March. A staged listing stands out in the flood — and in the winter months, staged photos keep a listing feeling warm when the light outside is grey.</p><p>That seasonality is the real argument for virtual home staging here. Physical home staging in January means scheduling a truck and a crew through Chicago weather; the furniture also has to stay, and pay rent, for however long the listing sits in a slow month. Staging the photos instead removes both problems — the cost is a one-time investment of {price:virtual-staging} a photo whether the home sells in a week or sits until spring.</p>",
        "local_heading": "Chicago home staging, done virtually for each buyer",
        "local_text": "<p>Designers stage clean contemporary for West Loop and River North condos, warm transitional for Lincoln Park and Lakeview vintage units, and family looks for the North Shore and western suburbs. MRED-ready files in 24 to 48 hours, disclosure guidance included, with full usage rights for the MLS, your website and social posts.</p><p>Two-flats and greystones get treated as the multi-unit listings they are: each unit staged to the buyer most likely to live in it, and the garden unit given enough light and warmth to read as a home rather than a basement.</p><p>Our design team works online, so there is no walk-through or consultation to schedule: order, upload your photos and your designer handles the layout, furnishings and accessories, creating a finished room from an empty one. Volume discounts apply automatically: 5% at 3+ photos, 10% at 6+, 15% at 11+ and 20% at 21+.</p>",
        "hoods_label": "Where we stage most",
        "hoods": "West Loop, River North, Lincoln Park, Lakeview, Logan Square, Pilsen, Hyde Park, Evanston, Oak Park, Naperville"
